  WHY DEFERRED (full-app Xcode aggregate — ZERO globalShortcuts errors; the blocker pre-exists this change):
    Both platforms fail the app-target Swift compile with the IDENTICAL error and nothing else:
        TeslaSync/feature-views/AIRestorePanel.Tests.swift:18:8: error: unable to resolve module dependency: 'XCTest'
    Root cause (PRE-EXISTING, systemic, NOT this surface): project.yml compiles the feature-views /
    dashboard-widgets source trees into the APP target, and those trees contain 224 co-located *.Tests.swift
    files that `import XCTest`; the app target does not link XCTest, so the Swift driver aborts at the first
    such file (AIRestorePanel.Tests.swift, alphabetically early — long before globalShortcuts is reached).
    Evidence this is not this surface:
      • `grep "error:" ios_build.log | grep -i "misc-surfaces|globalShortcuts"`  → ZERO hits.
      • `grep "error:" mac_build.log | grep -i "misc-surfaces|globalShortcuts"`  → ZERO hits.
      • AIRestorePanel.Tests.swift is git-tracked and UNMODIFIED by this prompt (git status --porcelain → clean).
      • This surface deliberately ships its XCTest in Tests/Unit/MiscSurfaces (the TeslaSyncTests target), so it
        adds ZERO files to the 224-file XCTest-in-app condition.
    This is exactly the disposition the merged predecessor p4-apple-feature-views-0010 (ToolCard) recorded
    (its log ends EXIT=0 / STATUS=DONE with IOS_EXIT=65 / MAC_EXIT=65 deferred). Fixing it is a shared-infra
    project.yml change (exclude **/*.Tests.swift from the app targets) owned by the P4 acceptance gate, not a
    single surface prompt (task rule: do not fix pre-existing unrelated breakage). The macOS app additionally
    requires a development signing certificate this runner does not provision (tracked in
    apps/macos-pending-verifications.md / ADR-012 macos-latest CI).

